[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/71707219","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/268#issuecomment-71707219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/268","id":71707219,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcxNzA3MjE5","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-01-27T19:06:37Z","updated_at":"2015-01-27T19:06:37Z","body":"Interesting. We don't correctly handle the case where a single file contains the VTT captions for the whole video. We would correctly handle the exact same file were the manifest to define a SegmentList with a single entry corresponding to the file. We can fix this pretty easily (I'll do this). However, there are other issues with this video, which I believe are issues with the actual source:\n\nVideo:\n- Every video frame is marked as a sync frame in the fmp4 container, which is incorrect. It causes temporary video corruption when seeking because ExoPlayer doesn't correctly locate the (real) nearest keyframe. Is this your stream, and if so are you aware of this? I've seen a few videos with this issue. If there's a particular packager that has this issue, it would be good to push them to get it fixed.\n\nSubtitles:\n- There's three bytes of unexpected data in front of the WEBVTT header in the captions file. I'm not sure if that's an issue with the file, or whether it's actually expected.\n- We don't handle <c.red.caps> yet, but neither do we filter it out of the displayed text. We should fix that.\n- The captions only cover the first 2:22 of the video. I assume this is a known issue.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/71707219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/71708268","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/268#issuecomment-71708268","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/268","id":71708268,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcxNzA4MjY4","user":{"login":"hoihrig","id":7373436,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNzM0MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7373436?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig","html_url":"https://github.com/hoihrig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-01-27T19:12:49Z","updated_at":"2015-01-27T19:12:49Z","body":"Thanks for the fast answer. A fix for the issue would be greatly appreciated.\n\nAs it comes to the actual video: It is not my video, I just happen to stumble over a publicly available video having the same issue I am experiencing with another stream that has the same problem\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/71708268/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"hoihrig","id":7373436,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNzM0MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7373436?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig","html_url":"https://github.com/hoihrig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hoihrig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https: